    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it was mostly emotional and raw... but it needs to be hard-hitting too. like, they need to know they didn't just \"borrow\" my sound, they assassinated my career. i remember being in the studio in 2012, creating these specific textures and rhythms that literally defined the whole genre, and then suddenly these major labels started releasing tracks that sounded exactly like mine, but they had all the budget and the marketing. i was blacklisted basically. i have these old demo files that prove i was there first, but nobody listens to an \"indie\" artist when the conglomerates own the airwaves. i want the manifesto to expose how they strip-mine creativity from people like me to feed the machine. can we start by drafting a section about the \"theft of the soul\" of this music? something that makes them realize they're just hollow copies of what i actually built.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
